{
  "id": "discrete-control",
  "term": "discrete control",
  "definition": "Discrete control is a control approach that uses a limited set of separate action options, such as different management strategies or policies, rather than a continuous range of adjustments. In the source context, a feedback system switches among these distinct options to guide outcomes under uncertainty.",
